# @file: ~/.config/VSCodium/User/.gitignore
# @mission: ignorar arquivos de runtime, estados internos e caches do VSCodium

### VSCodium / VS Code auto-generated folders
**/globalStorage/
**/workspaceStorage/
**/History/
**/Cache/
**/CachedData/
**/logs/
/profiles/**/chatLanguageModels.json
/profiles/**/extensions.json
/profiles/**/state.vscdb*
### Extensoes (Instaladas localmente)
/extensions/
**/extensions/
extensions_list.txt
profiles/*/extensions
zzz/pastas_DEFAULT_USER/

### AL ###
# Template for AL projects for Dynamics 365 Business Central
# launch.json folder # pode deixar os .vscode/
# Cache folder
.alcache/
# Symbols folder
.alpackages/
# Snapshots folder
.snapshots/
# Testing Output folder
.output/
# Extension App-file
*.app
# Rapid Application Development File
rad.json
# Translation Base-file
*.g.xlf
# License-files
*.bclicense
*.flf
# Test results file
TestResults.xml

# ==============================================================================
# @README_FILE
#
# @IMPORTANTE_PROFILE:
# - Regras com Wildcards (`/profiles/**/`) cobrem automaticamente qualquer hash
#   de perfil dinâmico criado pelo VSCodium (como 71cb6dfa), eliminando a necessidade
#   de mapear perfis individualmente no fim do arquivo.
# - Mantenha no versionador apenas os arquivos declarativos de configuração
#   (settings.json, keybindings.json) e a lista de extensões (extensions_list.txt).
#
# ==============================================================================
_controles/_backups_/Google-profile/extensions.json
